    "title": "Map artifacts and resources (AR)",
    "summary": "AR receiver: map artifacts and resources, command parameters, and limitations.",
    "keywords": [
      "AR",
      "!!AR",
      "AR:G",
      "AR:M^text^",
      "AR:V",
      "AR:X"
    ],
    "questions": [
      "Ресивер AR: артефакты и ресурсы на карте, параметры команд и ограничения.",
      "AR receiver: map artifacts and resources, command parameters, and limitations."
    ],
    "sourceRefs": [
      "old-help:rec-ar.htm"
    ],
    "text": "Receiver AR Receiver AR (artifacts or resources) !!AR#1/#2/#3:XXXX; - artifact or resource in X Y L coordinates (#1/#2/#3). Syntax extension: !!AR$:XXXX; - artifact OR resource in coordinates v[$], v[$+1], v[$+2] respectively. Used to modify the attributes of artifacts or resources at a specific position. Artifacts – type 5, scrolls with spells – type 93; resources – type 79. Artifacts and resources are numbered separately. Important note (show) Most of these commands will not affect artifact or the heap resources, if it does not have certain settings made in the Map Editor. This can be a simple setup of security for a resource or artifact. If artifact or resource does not have any special setting, a message about ERM error. You can use error output option statuses with commands UN:P904 P905, to avoid problems; you can also use the command OB:C to obtain a check number and process its value (but the command V$ will work correctly even if the scroll or resource does not have any installation). G#1/$2/$3 Set/check/get creatures - guards #1 – position (0..6) $2 – creature type $3 – number of creatures The team cannot turn on guards, it can only place them. Use option X to turn on. M^TEXT^ Set text message TEXT. The length of the text may exceed original. The message can contain any characters except \"^\" and \";\" M# Set the message text to the same as in global event under number #. M-1 Restore original message for artifact Mz# Set text from text variable z# M1/$ Set and get a text parameter. You can use this option when the M command is used to set a name or message. $ – text variable number = -1 – disable message (restore default) V$ Set/check/get a number spells in a scroll (if resource, then the number resource) Comment (show) For artifacts, this value specifies the lifting type: 0 – Artifact just rises 1 – Offer to buy artifact for 2000 coins 2 – Raising an artifact requires wisdom 3 – Leadership is required to pick up an artifact 4 – Offer to buy artifact for 2500 coins and 3 wood 5 – Offer to buy artifact for 3000 coins and 5 wood 6 – The artifact has security (another way to turn it on) All values greater than 6 make artifact unraveable. X# Enable guards if # is non-zero, otherwise disable. Checks for there are no security guards. Related reference OB Related commands and tables Artifact table · Game object table · Spell table · Resources · General game operations (UN) · Map objects (OB) · Creature table · Global events (GE)",
