    "text": "Receiver BU Receiver BU (universal battle parameters) !!BU:XXXX; - set/check/get some universal battle parameters. C?$ Used to accurately determine whether the battle is over or not $ = 1 if yes $ = 0 if not. Rational use in !?BG1; D#/?$ Receive or check position # for dead creatures ($ will contain the number of the dead stack). $ = stack number of dead creatures -1 if not at all creatures in position -2 if in position live stack E#/?$ Get or check $stack number on live creatures in positions #. If there are living creatures in this no position, $ = -1. G$ Set/check/get special landscapes and their bonuses in battle. $ – landscape type Comment (show) If you set this parameter before processing the battle, the game will select the correct background. If you change this value during battle, the background will not change, but the bonuses of the set terrain will still work. Mz# Add a message to the battle z# – z-variable with text Comment (show) This command is different from the command MM:M the fact that the MM:M message is only shown in the battle log, without saving it, when, as through BU:M, the text is shown and added to the event table, i.e. You can use the up and down arrows to scroll through and find that message later. Remember that you cannot eliminate the original text. O#/?$ Receive or check obstacle flags ($) for positions # to battlefield. $ = 0 if there are no obstacles Comment (show) The command can be used to check obstacle bits on a battlefield hex of interest. So, if there is a mine at the position, then we get $ = 9 (1+8) Note: for the Force field for the initial cell (bottom), the game sets the value $=35 (1+2+32), and for the rest - $=34 (2+32). The same goes for all obstacles set by the team. BF:O, in which the initial cell will have $=3 (1+2), and all others will have $=2 (when the obstacle occupies more than 1 cell). Additionally(show) When working with obstacles, the BU:O command cannot always help. For example, when you need to check the cells at the gate (during a siege). !!UN:C6919200/4/?y50; Battle Manager !!SN:E4625904/2/y50/[hex index]; We write down in v1 whether it is possible to stand in this place. 0 - possible, 1 - impossible. ; If the gate is not breached, the value for the attacker will be 1, otherwise - 0. R Update battlefield after any action Note: do not use this command in a trigger !?BF. Example (show) Unfortunately, this command does not update the active stack's movement grid. However, this can be done using the features ERA: ; Update shadow of possible movement after changing stack speed !!UN:C6919200/4/?y2; [Battle Manager] !!SN:E4797616/2/y2/0/1; [update battlefield grid] !!BU:R; S#1/#2/#3/#4/#5/#6 Summon creatures to battlefield #1 – creature type #2 – number of creatures #3 – position #4 – side (0 – left hero, 1 – right) #5 – hero slot number (-1 – missing (will disappear after the battle)) #6 – update (1 – yes, 0 – no) The position must be correct, free from other creatures and obstacles, and there cannot be more than 20 stacks on each side. T?$ Check if the battle has a tactical phase $ = 1 if yes $ = 0 if not V# Win the battle # - winning side 0 = right (defender) 1 = left (attacking) Related reference BF · BM Related commands and tables Battle actions (BG) · Battlefield hexes · BU:G special battle terrain · Battle hint text (MM) · Obstacle flags · Battlefield setup (BF) · ERM debugging and compatibility · Battlefield setup (BF) · Creature table <!-- ERA3-GENERATED:START --> ERA 3 changes These entries clarify or supersede historical behavior from the old ERM Help. - ERA 3.0.0, * — Fixed WoG bug with tactics detection on the very first round. Do not use BU:R in !?BR or !?FU(OnCombatRound) for zero round, because a few structures are not initialized at this moment and random crash may occur. First r… - ERA 3.0.0, + — SN:D may be used now in battle, being equal to BU:R. <!-- ERA3-GENERATED:END -->",
