    "text": "Receiver DW Receiver DW (home creatures) !!DW#1/#2/#3:XXXX; - creatures' home in X Y L. Housing – type 17 and 20. G#1/$2/$3 Set guard creatures: #1 – slot number (0..6) #2 – creature type (-1 – no) #3 – number of creatures M#1/$2/$3 Set creatures to hire: #1 – slot (0..3) - you can install up to four different creatures in one dwelling #2 – creature type (-1 – disable slot) #3 – quantity to hire O$ Install owner $ (no update) Extended syntax: O$/1 Transfer control to another player, $ – owner Comment: Unlike DW:O$, this syntax changes the owner of the dwelling by updating the internal game structures (all indicators in the weekly growth statistics in the towns of the corresponding faction are adjusted; the viewing radius around the dwelling is updated). Note: For correct operation of your scripts in network mode, use only this syntax. Related reference OB · UN Related commands and tables Creature dwellings on the map · Creature table · Player colors",
