    "text": "Receiver EX Receiver EX (stack experience) !!EX$1/$2:XXXX; - creature stack experience. $1 – hero number (0..155, -1), $2 – slot number (0..6). Syntax extension 1: !!EX$1/$2/$3/$4:XXXX; $1 – X (0…) $2 – Y (0…) $3 – L (0 - Surface, 1 - Underground) $4 – slot number (this position may contain hero, town, garrison or mine) Syntax extension 2: !!EX$1/$2/$3/$4/$5:XXXX; $1 – X $2 – Y $3 – L $4 – slot number (0..6) $5 – object type 1 = hero 2 = town 3 = mine 4 = garrison other number = any higher listed If you use 4 parameters, the fifth one is default is in the \"first found\" state. The search proceeds in the following order: heroes, towns, mines, garrisons. A$1/$2/$3 Set/check/get information on the stack: $1 – creature type (255 is an empty slot) $2 – number of creatures $3 – amount of experience the creature has C$1/$2/$3[/$4/$5/$6] Connect stacks $1 – source stack type $1 = 0 - from the hero $2 – hero number (-1 – current) $3 – hero slot (0..6) [$4] – display warning (see below) $1=1 – hero in coordinates $1=2 – town in coordinates $1=3 – mine in coordinates $1=4 – garrison in coordinates $2 – X-position $3 – Y-position $4 – level (0 = Surface, 1 = Underground) $5 – army slot (0..6) [$6] – show warning Results This command will set the variable v1 to: -1 if they are different creatures (cannot be combined) 0 if an error occurred (cannot be combined) 1 if the combination was successful. Comment (show) This command will add the original stack to the army slot, along with the combination parameters. All experience will be distributed equally to all soldiers, artifacts are summed up. If you install warning type to 1 (default 0), you won't get a message that these stacks are different. Example 1: Hero visits the object and its stack 3 is added to stack 1 (they must be the same type): !?OB5/3/0; !!EX-1/1:C0/-1/3; Example 2: You visit the object and your current hero “adds” the first stack in town (input 3/2/0) to stack #3. !?OB5/3/0; !!EX-1/3:C2/3/2/0/1; E$ Set/check/get the experience of creatures: $ – creature experience N$ Set/check/get number of creatures $ – quantity R$1/$2 Set/check/get artifact and option $1 – artifact number (available only artifact #156) $2 – artifact option (0..8) 0 +2 health plus double current health bonus in combat 1 +2 attack plus double current attack bonus in combat 2 +2 defense plus double current combat defense bonus 3 +1 damage plus double the current minimum and maximum damage bonus in combat 4 +1 speed plus double current combat speed bonus 5 +50% squad experience per battle 6 Reduces target's defense by 25% 7 25% chance to block 50% damage 8 2 additional answers Syntax extension: R$1/$2/$3/$4 $1 – whether there is artifact or not (0 = no, 1 = yes) $2 – artifact number (currently only 156) $3 – artifact subtype (options 0..15 – not all are used yet) $4 – number of copies of the artifact (0..3) T$ Set/check/get creature type $ – creature type (255 is an empty slot) Related reference EA Related commands and tables Hero table · Creature table · Artifact table",
