    "text": "Receiver FC Receiver FC (town faction management) !!FC#:XXXX; – changing the attributes of town factions # (0..9). Comment (show) This receiver was conceived not so much for changing town templates, but for working in tandem with associative arrays. However, thanks to it, many things can now actually be implemented without plugins and patches. B0/$ Set/check/get creature, purchased at the forge. B1/$ Set/check/get the essence of shown in the forge. Example: !!FC0:B0/7 B1/7; You can buy a Crusader in the Castle forge C$1/$2/$3/$4 Coordinates of buildings on the town screen. $1 – building number $2 – number of frames in DEF $3/$4 – X/Y positions. Comment: if some parameter does not need to be modified, the values -1 or d0 can be used. D$1/$2 Set/check/get the priority of displaying buildings. $1 – array element index $2 – building number H#/$1/$2 Setting the parameters of the “Horde #” structure ($1 - unimproved creature, $2 – improved creature). # = 0 – increase in horde structure 1 # = 1 - increase in horde structure 2 # = 2 – level of creatures in the horde structure 1 # = 3 - level of creatures in horde structure 2 Example: !!FC2:H0/10/10; Sculptor's wings increase the growth of Gargoyles by 10 H4/$1/$2/$3 Type of simple $2 and improved $3 creatures in a $1 (1/2) horde structure. M Get the width of the ditch (0..2; 0 = no ditch) into the variable v1. M0/# Set ditch type (2, 1, none). M1/$ Set/check/get damage from a moat. R$1/$2 Set/check/get resources $1 (0..6) in the resource storage (where $2 is the quantity). Example: !!FC1:R4/1000; Stronghold Vault brings 1000 crystals S$ Set/check/get creature in the Arrow Tower. Example: !!FC8:S8; There will now be Monks in the Conjugation Towers T$ Set/check/to obtain the native soil of the fraction (0..9). Related reference CA",
