        "text": "A trigger selects when code runs. For example, !?BA0; responds to battle initialization. A receiver specifies an operation: !!HE accesses heroes, !!OW players, and !!IF messages and flags. The same two-letter code can identify a trigger and a receiver; its prefix determines the role. A handler extends to the next trigger declaration. Multiple handlers of the same event execute in sequence."
