        "text": "# Meaning Ability 0 1 Wide - occupies two cells. 1 2 Creature can fly. 2 4 Creature can fire. If you give this ability to a non-shooter, you will receive several error messages (\"invalid resource\"). Possible only with additional graphics. 3 8 Extended attack radius (two cells). It's like the breath of a dragon. This flag does not work for shooting, only in hand-to-hand combat. 4 16 Alive creature. Makes the creature sensitive to Blessing, Joy, Death Wave, Morale and other things that work only for the living. 5 32 Catapult (specialty X1). Creature can attack the town walls. 6 64 Siege weapon. Can't move. Teleporting will result in a crash from the game. Stack is not required to kill to achieve victory. There is no indication of the number of creatures near the squad. 7 128 King 1 is all level 7 creatures and neutral dragons, not belonging to KING 2 or KING 3, creatures carrying additional. spell damage Slayer. 8 256 King 2 - Angels, Archangels, Devils, Archdevils; creatures carrying additional spell damage Slayer adv. or higher level. 9 512 King 3 - Giants, Titans; creatures carrying additional spell damage Slayer exp. level. 10 1024 Immunity to mind spells (like Sadness, Frenzy, etc.). 11 2048 Creature - 35 (Arch Mage), 74 (Beholder), 75 (Evil Eye). The shot animation with this flag becomes a continuous straight beam. 12 4096 No melee penalties (for shooters) 13 8192 The game never checks. Perhaps it was used before, but has now lost its meaning. 14 16384 Immunity to fire spells, incl. positive (Ifrits). 15 32768 Double strike (upgraded Crossbowmen or Crusaders). 16 65536 No answer (Cerberus or Hydra). 17 131072 No morale penalties (Elementals, Golems). 18 262144 Undead (all Necropolis creatures, creature with this flag have no morality, takes damage from Destroy Undead and does not take damage from Death Wave). 19 524288 Attacks everyone around, does not work together with Dragon's Breath. 20 1048576 Extended firing radius. This is a Magog ability/Lychees/Power Lich. Used only by AI, has no value to the player. 21 2097152 Stack does not get the right to move during the battle. Once the battle is over, stack will disappear. Stack does not require killing to achieve victory. There is no indication of the number of creatures near the squad. Immunity to some spells. This flag is automatically set when creature dies. If you set this flag yourself, then removing it will resurrect creature. When receiving damage while in a “dead” state, the number of creatures and health of the last creature on the stack is reduced. Therefore, after resurrection there can be 0 creatures. But this does not prevent you from installing using BM:N as many creatures as needed. If creature really died, then removing the flag creature will not resurrect, but can lead to various failures in the AI. Teleports correctly. 22 4194304 At the end of the battle or if you die, stack will disappear. Elementals summoned by a spell in battle have this flag. 23 8388608 If stack receives any damage, it will die. Stack is colored blue (as with the spell Clone). 24 16777216 In this round of battle, the unit received morale 25 33554432 Stack is in a waiting state. 26 67108864 In this round of battle, stack has already taken an action. 27 134217728 Stack is in the protective position. 28 268435456 The flag is displayed to the stack when it has been sacrificed. The squad's body disappears upon death. 29 536870912 Creatures with this flag do not change their color when cloned or petrified"
