    "text": "Trigger LE Trigger LE (local event) !?LE#1/#2/#3; - triggers when visiting a local event at certain coordinates, the event is not changed, it is used only as trigger. #1/#2/#3 = X Y L, respectively An event MUST exist at the specified point. See also: receiver !!LE Post-trigger LE !$LE#1/#2/#3; - local event, post-trigger. This trigger works like !?LE, but after visiting the event. Example: ZVSE !?LE10/10/0; - trigger !!IF:M^Trigger LE triggered^; ; the message will appear before the event properties configured in the editor are initialized !$LE10/10/0; - post-trigger !!IF:M^Post-trigger LE^; ; the message will appear after executing the event properties configured in the editor When it fires X/Y/level selects an existing local map event. !? runs before its standard effects; !$ runs afterwards. Declaration !?LE#1/#2/#3; / !$LE#1/#2/#3; Limitations and ordering The event must exist at the location. A one-shot event may disappear after visiting; account for LE’s error flag. Related reference Event catalog · Conditions · Functions Related commands and tables Local map events (LE) <!-- ERA3-GENERATED:START --> ERA 3 changes These entries clarify or supersede historical behavior from the old ERM Help. - ERA 3.4.0, + — Implemented two universal events for handling human local events: \"OnBeforeLocalEvent\" and \"OnAfterLocalEvent\". They occur before any !?LE/!$LE trigger respecively and receive 3 parameters: x, y and z coordinates. Exampl… <!-- ERA3-GENERATED:END -->",
