    "text": "Trigger MW Trigger MW (wandering creatures) !?MW#; - trigger for wandering creatures. !?MW0; - Called when reaching a destination or hero. !?MW1; - Called when the stray creature dies. !?MW0 - is called on the next turn, after reaching a point or attacking the hero, and only if the corresponding flag is set. v997 contains the number of the wandering creature - the trigger caller. !?MW1 - summoned during the turn after the death of the creature. Fires only if the corresponding flag is set. v997 contains the number of the killed roaming creature. See also: receiver !!MW When it fires 0 reaching a destination/hero, 1 monster death. v997 is the wandering-monster ID. Corresponding MW settings must enable these events. Declaration !?MW0; / !?MW1; ERA names and aliases ERM Name ID MW0 OnWanderingMonsterReach 30305 MW1 OnWanderingMonsterDeath 30306 Limitations and ordering The classic implementation fires on the next turn after arrival or death, not immediately. Related reference Event catalog · Conditions · Functions Related commands and tables Wandering monsters (MW)",
