    "text": "Receiver TH Trigger TL(real time timer) !?TL#; - Real time timer. # = 0 - fires every second # = 1 - triggers every 2 seconds # = 2 - triggers every 5 seconds # = 3 - triggers every 10 seconds # = 4 - triggers every 60 seconds Example: To see how this works, use the following code: !?TL0; !!IF:L^1 second ticked^; !?TL1; !!IF:L^2 seconds ticked^; !?TL2; !!IF:L^5 seconds have passed^; !?TL3; !!IF:L^Already 10 seconds^; !?TL4; !!IF:L^Exactly a minute has passed!^; When it fires Index 0 means 1 second, 1 means 2 seconds, 2 means 5 seconds, 3 means 10 seconds, and 4 means 60 seconds. Declaration !?TL#; ERA names and aliases ERM Name ID TL0 OnEverySecond 30900 TL1 OnEvery2Seconds 30901 TL2 OnEvery5Seconds 30902 TL3 OnEvery10Seconds 30903 TL4 OnEveryMinute 30904 Limitations and ordering These are not game days. Do not treat wall-clock timing as an automatically synchronized condition for multiplayer gameplay. Related reference Event catalog · Conditions · Functions Related commands and tables ERM debugging and compatibility",
