        "text": "+ added · lines 44–66: Implemented detailed game context dumping in \"exception context.txt\" on crash. The format is the following: > Game context: [Dialog Name] dialog … Implemented detailed game context dumping in \"exception context.txt\" on crash. The format is the following: > Game context: [Dialog Name] dialog (tag1, tag2...) Possible dialog names: \"Adventure Map\", \"Adventure Actions\", \"Adventure Popup\", \"Combat Settings\", \"Combat Log\", \"Combat\", \"Dialog\", \"Dimension Door\", \"Sink Ship,\", \"Hero\", \"Hill Fort\", \"Hero LevelUp\", \"Kingdom Overview\", \"Puzzle\", \"Journal\", \"Dwelling\", \"Altar of Sacrifice\", \"Skeleton Transformer,\", \"Scenario Info\", \"Saving\", \"Spell Book\", \"Hero Meeting\", \"Adventure Settings\", \"Select Town\", \"Town\", \"Thieves Guild\", \"Town Hall\", \"Mage Guild,\", \"Leave Creatures\", \"Garrison\", \"Blacksmith\", \"Shipyard / WoG DL\", \"Building Info\", \"Tavern\", \"Fort\", \"Resource Exchange\", \"Resource Transfer,\", \"Buy Artifacts\", \"Sell Artifacts\", \"Freelancers Guild\", \"University\", \"Monster Info\", \"World Overview\". By default singleplayer human turn is assumed. Possible tags: - AI turn: on AI turn only - HotSeat: if game type is Hot Seat - Network: for any network game type (TCP, direct connection, lobby, etc) - Host: if current PC is a host in a network game - Client: if current PC is a clent in a network game - Combat if combat takes place - AI vs AI: for full AI combat - AI vs Human: combat, where AI hero attacked human - Human vs AI: combat, where human hero attack AI - Human vs Human: combat, where human hero attack human"
